<stack-static>
    <statement><p><p>Each table is meant to be a probability distribution. For each, choose the right description.</p><p>Table 1</p><tabular border="1" style="border-collapse:collapse;text-align:center;"><row><cell style="padding:4px 10px;"><m>x</m></cell><cell style="padding:4px 10px;">1</cell><cell style="padding:4px 10px;">2</cell><cell style="padding:4px 10px;">3</cell></row><row><cell style="padding:4px 10px;"><m>P(X = x)</m></cell><cell style="padding:4px 10px;"><m>{0.2}</m></cell><cell style="padding:4px 10px;"><m>{0.5}</m></cell><cell style="padding:4px 10px;"><m>{0.3}</m></cell></row></tabular><div><ol marker="(1)">
<li>No: the probabilities do not add up to 1.</li>
<li>Yes, it is a probability distribution.</li>
<li>No: a probability is less than 0 or more than 1.</li>
</ol>  </div><p>Table 2</p><tabular border="1" style="border-collapse:collapse;text-align:center;"><row><cell style="padding:4px 10px;"><m>x</m></cell><cell style="padding:4px 10px;">1</cell><cell style="padding:4px 10px;">2</cell><cell style="padding:4px 10px;">3</cell></row><row><cell style="padding:4px 10px;"><m>P(X = x)</m></cell><cell style="padding:4px 10px;"><m>{0.3}</m></cell><cell style="padding:4px 10px;"><m>{0.4}</m></cell><cell style="padding:4px 10px;"><m>{0.2}</m></cell></row></tabular><div><ol marker="(1)">
<li>No: the probabilities do not add up to 1.</li>
<li>Yes, it is a probability distribution.</li>
<li>No: a probability is less than 0 or more than 1.</li>
</ol>  </div><p>Table 3</p><tabular border="1" style="border-collapse:collapse;text-align:center;"><row><cell style="padding:4px 10px;"><m>x</m></cell><cell style="padding:4px 10px;">1</cell><cell style="padding:4px 10px;">2</cell><cell style="padding:4px 10px;">3</cell></row><row><cell style="padding:4px 10px;"><m>P(X = x)</m></cell><cell style="padding:4px 10px;"><m>{0.6}</m></cell><cell style="padding:4px 10px;"><m>{-0.1}</m></cell><cell style="padding:4px 10px;"><m>{0.5}</m></cell></row></tabular><div><ol marker="(1)">
<li>No: the probabilities do not add up to 1.</li>
<li>Yes, it is a probability distribution.</li>
<li>No: a probability is less than 0 or more than 1.</li>
</ol>  </div></p></statement>
    <solution><p><p>A table is a probability distribution when every probability is from 0 to 1 and the probabilities add up to exactly 1. Check both.</p><p>Table 1: the probabilities add to <m>{1}</m>. Every value is from 0 to 1, so it is a probability distribution.</p><p>Table 2: the probabilities add to <m>{0.9}</m>. That is not 1, so it is not a probability distribution.</p><p>Table 3: the probabilities add to <m>{1}</m>. They add to 1, but <m>{-0.1}</m> is negative, so it cannot be a probability: this is not a probability distribution.</p></p></solution>
    <answer><p><m>(2)</m></p></answer>
    <answer><p><m>(1)</m></p></answer>
    <answer><p><m>(3)</m></p></answer>
